            <ArticleTitle>Hemoperitoneum secondary to intercostal arterial bleeding in a trauma patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">rjw194</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/jscr/rjw194</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Blunt trauma resulting in rib fractures can be associated with hemothorax, pneumothorax, pulmonary contusions or less frequently chest and abdominal wall hematomas. Our case describes the first report of hemoperitoneum secondary to intercostal arterial bleeding from blunt trauma in a patient on anticoagulation.</AbstractText>
